WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:02.569
Because I like
to check in with you.

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:03.803
'Cause it's been about a year.
-Yeah.

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.237
-And this is the only time
we see each other.

00:00:05.237 --> 00:00:06.506
-It really is.
We're like party friends

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:07.707
except it's not even
a party friend.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:09.909
It's like a -- It's weirder.
-Yeah, we are.

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:11.143
It's weirder
than even party friends.

00:00:11.143 --> 00:00:12.412
-It's weirder
than a party friend.

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:14.146
-But I do want to check in,
'cause you were here

00:00:14.146 --> 00:00:15.715
about a year ago,
and you were very happy.

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.550
You were, like, proud,
and I felt like you thought

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.051
you were becoming an adult.

00:00:19.051 --> 00:00:21.187
-I've heard whisperings of what
you're talking about earlier.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.355
-Well, you were talking about

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:23.923
you had moved in to
a new apartment,

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:25.458
and then you said
you were thinking

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:26.860
about getting a dog and a car.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.595
So I'd like an update.
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:00:29.595 --> 00:00:32.165
Well, I don't have a car.
-Okay.

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:34.166
-I actually don't have
a license right now.

00:00:34.166 --> 00:00:35.868
-Oh, no.
Why don't you have a license?

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:37.537
-'Cause I lost it.

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:38.704
-Okay.
-That's true.

00:00:38.704 --> 00:00:41.140
-Okay, but you can
just get a new one.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.443
-Yes, I can.
I have an appointment.

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:44.744
[ Laughs ] This is all real.

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:46.813
I have an appointment
next Monday in Santa Monica.

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:48.348
-Oh, so you have to go to a DMV.

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:50.383
-Yeah.
And just have a face-to-face.

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:53.786
I got an e-mail that I can take,
like, another photo if I want,

00:00:53.786 --> 00:00:55.955
which I'd like to
'cause my license photo isn't --

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.156
It's not cute.

00:00:57.156 --> 00:00:58.424
-What do you think went wrong
the last time

00:00:58.424 --> 00:01:00.560
when you took the photo?
-I think I was too excited.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.761
-Okay.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:03.996
-I was, like, really --
I was, like, too --

00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:06.299
-It is such a bummer
when you get too excited

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:07.767
for a license, especially when

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.502
you get pulled over
for speeding.

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:11.271
-Ugh!
-Because when you give that,

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:12.972
it looks like you were
definitely speeding.

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:15.308
Like, if you're a guy who...

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:18.344
couldn't wait to be
a legal driver.

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.113
So you don't have
a license or a car.

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:22.849
So that one seems like that's a
step backwards from a year ago.

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:24.550
-Yeah. So hopefully
a year from now

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.018
I'll at least have a license.

00:01:26.018 --> 00:01:28.354
-A new license. Okay.
-So I don't have a car.

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:30.289
I am going to get a dog.
-Okay. So you have not --

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:32.024
In a full year,
you haven't gotten one yet.

00:01:32.024 --> 00:01:33.826
-Haven't gotten a dog.
Haven't gotten the car.

00:01:33.826 --> 00:01:35.261
-Lost a license.
-Right. Yes. Lost a license.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.829
-And do you know what kind
of dog you're getting?

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:39.632
-So maybe we've moved backwards.
Yeah, I do.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:41.034
I'm getting a French bulldog.

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:42.869
-Okay, great.
That's very exciting.

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:44.804
-I know.
They make me feel that way, too.

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:47.140
-Have you ever had a French
bulldog in your life before?

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.541
-No.
-Okay. Do you know --

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:50.610
Like, do you have any sense
of the timeline

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.211
of when you're going to get one?

00:01:52.211 --> 00:01:54.981
-Well, uh...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:56.282
Yeah, like the middle of August.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:58.351
-"Well, the problem
is I got to drive there,

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:00.820
and that's a whole thing
because of my license."

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.955
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:05.624
Maybe they could just -- They're
gonna give this dog your address

00:02:05.624 --> 00:02:09.028
and say, "It might be faster if
you just find your way there."

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:11.364
-"Go find her."
Lassie, come home.

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:14.200
-Do you have -- Do you want
a boy dog, a girl dog?

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.402
-A girl dog.
-Do you have a name picked out?

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.404
Or are you gonna wait until
you actually lay eyes on it?

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:20.039
-No, I'm thinking about it.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:22.542
-I like --
I think, uh, like Tank.

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:25.177
-Okay, for...
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:25.177 --> 00:02:26.446
-That seems like --

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:28.147
I mean, again, you know,
look, who am I to say?

00:02:28.147 --> 00:02:29.449
That seems like a boy's name.

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:31.317
But I guess -- I don't know.
-I know.

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:33.286
-But, again, maybe
a girl bulldog doesn't --

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:34.587
-But I like it.
-Yeah. What does she care?

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:35.955
-She doesn't care.
-Yeah, it's just a noise.

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:37.523
-And where --
It's gender-normative.

00:02:37.523 --> 00:02:39.959
Like, it's passé. Lame.
-Exactly.

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:42.327
Also, she's French. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:42.327 --> 00:02:43.663
What does that even mean?

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:45.931
-[ French accent ]
It's so American to say

00:02:45.931 --> 00:02:48.033
Tank is a boy's name.

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:51.203
Tank is a name
that can be anyone's name!

00:02:51.203 --> 00:02:54.306
-She just doesn't
play those games.

00:02:54.306 --> 00:02:56.008
-One of my favorite things
we've ever talked about

00:02:56.008 --> 00:02:57.743
is your first New York City
apartment sounded like

00:02:57.743 --> 00:03:00.413
the worst apartment,
or the smallest apartment.

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:02.348
-Well, it was.
-What was the --

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:04.717
There was something.
The bed was something?

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:06.419
The bed was in the kitchen?
-Yes, the bed is in the --

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:07.787
Well, it went --
I mean, it was one room.

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:08.888
-Oh, right.
Now I remember the word.

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:09.922
-It was one room.
-Yeah.

00:03:09.922 --> 00:03:11.190
-So it was a bitchen.
-A bitchen.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.960
-The kitchen and the bedroom
were the same room.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:16.696
So we had -- We just were like,
"Come over to our bitchen."

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:18.397
-I will say...
-It's the bedroom.

00:03:18.397 --> 00:03:20.299
-...that if you got asked
to come over

00:03:20.299 --> 00:03:22.768
to a bitchen apartment,
you'd be like, "Awesome!"

00:03:22.768 --> 00:03:24.871
I think it's gonna be like
a wraparound penthouse.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:27.806
And meanwhile it's like --
-It's like a...

00:03:27.806 --> 00:03:30.843
couch that you're sleeping on,
with, like, a pull-out --

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:33.612
with one of the things,
a door over the stove.

00:03:33.612 --> 00:03:36.248
-Yeah. Right. "I went back to
this girl's bitchen apartment."

00:03:36.248 --> 00:03:38.451
"How'd it go?" "I knocked
my head out on a sink."

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:40.186
-Yeah. No, it's not.
It wasn't safe.

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:42.322
The truth of the apartment
is that it wasn't safe.

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:44.591
-But you recently got in --

00:03:44.591 --> 00:03:46.159
Your roommate
got in touch with you?

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:48.294
-Oh, my roommate from that time
is one of my best friends.

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:49.829
-Okay. Still?
-Yeah. Hey, Tommy.

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:51.497
-Okay.
-I've never done that before.

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:53.532
-And he found something
from back in the day?

00:03:53.532 --> 00:03:56.068
-Yeah, he recently
found this three days ago.

00:03:56.068 --> 00:03:59.605
And I was so excited I was
going to come and see you.

00:03:59.605 --> 00:04:01.707
I -- Seriously. I got this --

00:04:01.707 --> 00:04:04.376
And also the subject heading
was "Dark Days."

00:04:04.376 --> 00:04:06.045
-Dark days. So this was --

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:08.047
Now, this is somebody
that you've managed
to stay friends with.

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:10.049
-Oh, for like --
-You guys got through this.

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:12.085
-I mean,
by the skin of our teeth.

00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:14.254
-This is a legal document
that he wrote up.

00:04:14.254 --> 00:04:16.021
This is a roommate agreement.
-Yes.

00:04:16.021 --> 00:04:17.657
-Was he a lawyer?
-No.

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:19.925
He's an -- he was an --
He was an actor.

00:04:19.925 --> 00:04:21.460
-Okay.
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:24.229
-There is so much legalese
to this.

00:04:24.229 --> 00:04:26.365
I can not stress
how crazy this is.

00:04:26.365 --> 00:04:28.768
-Wait. And you didn't even see
there is room

00:04:28.768 --> 00:04:30.236
for both of us to sign
at the bottom.

00:04:30.236 --> 00:04:32.438
And he wasn't gonna -- I don't
know what he was going to do.

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:35.040
-This is my favorite one.
Hold on.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.310
"Both parties
must treat the other

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:39.579
with courtesy and respect,
regardless of their state

00:04:39.579 --> 00:04:41.513
of inebriation, exhaustion,

00:04:41.513 --> 00:04:43.715
or general
non-collaborative mood."

00:04:43.715 --> 00:04:46.218
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:46.218 --> 00:04:49.722
That is -- That's --
-Isn't that amazing?

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:51.624
-It's amazing that you had --
like, basically signing

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:53.092
a legal document
saying you're gonna --

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:55.027
No matter how drunk you are,
you have to treat somebody

00:04:55.027 --> 00:04:56.128
with courtesy and respect.

00:04:56.128 --> 00:04:58.164
-Respect. Yeah. Dignity.
We're all humans.

00:04:58.164 --> 00:05:01.868
-The amount that he says
"both parties" is fantastic.

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:04.236
I'm so happy to hear
he was also an actor.

00:05:04.236 --> 00:05:05.504
This is written like somebody

00:05:05.504 --> 00:05:06.872
who watched a lot
of "Law &amp; Order."

00:05:06.872 --> 00:05:08.841
-His dad's a lawyer.
-Oh, his dad's a lawyer.

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:10.676
-So I feel like
he might have had his dad

00:05:10.676 --> 00:05:11.910
proofread it or something.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:13.646
-This is --
I mean, this is the best.

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:17.050 line:0%
-He had bullet points.
-"Hitherto."

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:19.017 line:0%
-Oh, my God!
I didn't even see that!

00:05:19.017 --> 00:05:22.788 line:0%
-"This hitherto serves as
a binding roommate agreement."

00:05:22.788 --> 00:05:24.957 line:0%
-"Not to be made null or void

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:27.126 line:0%
unless agreed upon
by both parties."

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:30.196
I mean, what is that? He was,
like, a 22-year-old actor.

00:05:30.196 --> 00:05:31.897
Let me see that.
-It's so great.

00:05:31.897 --> 00:05:33.499
Like, what I like
to picture is

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:36.168
you coming home super-wasted,
being an asshole,

00:05:36.168 --> 00:05:38.370
and him saying, like,
"Hey! Our agreement!"

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:41.807
You're like, "[Bleep] you!
My kitchen's a bedroom!

00:05:41.807 --> 00:05:43.976
I don't care!

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:45.144
You signed an agreement!

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:47.379
-"[Bleep] you!
My kitchen's a bedroom!"

00:05:47.379 --> 00:05:49.148
-You signed an agreement!
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:51.784
-You're in a
non-collaborative mood!"

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:53.986
-No, that was --
I read that, and I died.

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:56.589
That's my favorite.
That's my favorite thing ever.

00:05:56.589 --> 00:05:59.058
-That is the nicest way to say
somebody's being a jerk.

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:01.127
Yeah, it's a really nice way
to put some of my --

00:06:01.127 --> 00:06:03.128
I guess what it's like
to live with me sometimes.

00:06:03.128 --> 00:06:04.230
-Yeah. Non-collaborative.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:06.366
-A generally
non-collaborative partner.

